        "doc_b2": {
          "type": "clause",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Orders and acceptance",
            "body": "<p>An order is an offer to buy. It becomes a contract when we send the dispatch confirmation, not when the payment clears and not when the order confirmation arrives.</p> <ul><li>We may decline an order if a piece sells out between your checkout and our picking it.</li><li>We may limit quantities on a drop so that one buyer cannot take the whole run.</li><li>If we decline, you are refunded in full within three business days, to the original payment method.</li></ul>",
            "table": "",
            "table_first": true
          }
        },
        "doc_b3": {
          "type": "clause",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Prices and payment",
            "body": "<p>Prices are in US dollars and exclude sales tax, which is calculated at checkout against the delivery address. Payment is taken in full at checkout through our payment processor; we never see or store your card number.</p> <p>If a price is listed incorrectly through an obvious error, we contact you before dispatch and you may confirm at the corrected price or cancel for a full refund.</p>",
            "table": "",
            "table_first": true
          }
        },
        "doc_b4": {
          "type": "clause",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Delivery and risk",
            "body": "<p>Risk passes to you on delivery to the address you gave us. Title passes when payment has cleared in full. Delivery estimates are estimates; a carrier delay is not a breach of these terms, though it may still entitle you to a return under the section below.</p>",
            "table": "",
            "table_first": true
          }
        },
        "doc_b5": {
          "type": "clause",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Returns, refunds and your statutory rights",
            "body": "<p>Our returns policy sits alongside your rights under Michigan and federal law and does not replace them. Nothing in these terms limits liability for fraud, for death or personal injury caused by negligence, or for anything else that cannot lawfully be limited.</p> <p>The practical detail lives in the Shipping and Returns page, which forms part of these terms.</p>",
